workedExamples.solution_text:
Half the base edge is $6\text{ cm}$. The perpendicular height and half the base edge form a right-angled triangle with the slant height $l$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0)--(0,3.2)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.22)--(0.22,0.22)--(0.22,0);
\path (0,1.6) node[left] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.2,0) node[below] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.2,1.6) node[right] {$l$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned} l^{2}&=8^{2}+6^{2}\\l^{2}&=100\\l&=10\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

Area of the base:
$\begin{aligned} A_{\text{base}}&=12\times12\\&=144\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Area of the four triangular faces:
$\begin{aligned} A_{\text{triangles}}&=4\times\left(\frac12\times12\times10\right)\\&=240\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Total surface area:
$\begin{aligned} SA&=144+240\\&=384\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Base edge:
$\begin{aligned} s&=\sqrt{100}\\&=10\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

Area of the four triangular faces:
$\begin{aligned} A_{\text{triangles}}&=600-100\\&=500\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Area of one triangular face:
$\begin{aligned} A_{\text{face}}&=500\div4\\&=125\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Find the slant height:
$\begin{aligned} 125&=\frac12\times10\times l\\125&=5l\\l&=25\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

Half the base edge is $5\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(1,0)--(0,3.4)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.18)--(0.18,0.18)--(0.18,0);
\path (0,1.7) node[left] {$h$};
\path (0.5,0) node[below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.5,1.7) node[right] {$25\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned} h^{2}+5^{2}&=25^{2}\\h^{2}&=25^{2}-5^{2}\\h^{2}&=600\\h&=\sqrt{600}\\h&\approx24.5\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

The faces on the $10\text{ cm}$ edges use half the $8\text{ cm}$ width. The faces on the $8\text{ cm}$ edges use half the $10\text{ cm}$ length.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.2,0)--(0,3.6)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);
\path (0,1.8) node[left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.6,0) node[below] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.6,1.8) node[right] {$l_{1}$};
\draw (4,0)--(5.5,0)--(4,3.6)--cycle;
\draw (4,0.2)--(4.2,0.2)--(4.2,0);
\path (4,1.8) node[left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (4.75,0) node[below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (4.75,1.8) node[right] {$l_{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the two slant heights:
$\begin{aligned} l_{1}^{2}&=12^{2}+4^{2}\\l_{1}^{2}&=160\\l_{1}&=\sqrt{160}\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned} l_{2}^{2}&=12^{2}+5^{2}\\l_{2}^{2}&=169\\l_{2}&=13\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

Area of the base:
$\begin{aligned} A_{\text{base}}&=10\times8\\&=80\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Area of the triangles on the $10\text{ cm}$ edges:
$\begin{aligned} A_{1}&=2\times\left(\frac12\times10\times\sqrt{160}\right)\\&=10\sqrt{160}\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Area of the triangles on the $8\text{ cm}$ edges:
$\begin{aligned} A_{2}&=2\times\left(\frac12\times8\times13\right)\\&=104\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

Keep the exact slant height until the final rounding.
$\begin{aligned} SA&=80+10\sqrt{160}+104\\&\approx310.5\text{ cm}^{2}\end{aligned}$

